response:
 A clock makes a full rotation of 360^\circ in one hour, or 60 minutes.  Therefore, in one minute, 1^\circ moves past the hour hand by $360^\circ /60=\boxed{6}^\circ$. Since it is now 7 a.m., the minute hand has moved 7 rotations past the hour hand, where each rotation ($360^\circ$) is $7\times 6^\circ=42^\circ$.

